---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import Nav from '../components/Nav.astro';
import Footer from '../components/Footer.astro';
---

<Layout
  title="Privacy Policy — Crystal Lattice"
  description="Crystal Lattice privacy policy. Local-first software — your data stays on your machine."
>
  <Nav />
  <main class="prose-page">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="header">
        <p class="label">Legal</p>
        <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
        <p class="meta">Effective date: May 2025</p>
      </div>

      <div class="content">
        <section>
          <h2>The short version</h2>
          <p>
            Crystal Lattice is local-first software. It runs on your machine. Your conversations,
            sessions, and agent history are stored on your own filesystem and are never sent to us.
            We don't have servers that store your data. We don't have accounts. We don't have a cloud.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2>What Crystal Lattice collects</h2>
          <p>The Crystal Lattice CLI and server software collect nothing on our behalf. Specifically:</p>
          <ul>
            <li>All session data, message history, and agent configuration is stored locally on your machine in the working directory you specify.</li>
            <li>No telemetry, analytics, or usage data is transmitted to Crystal Lattice from the CLI or server software.</li>
            <li>No account creation is required. We have no user database.</li>
          </ul>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2>AI provider requests</h2>
          <p>
            When you run an agent session, Crystal Lattice sends your messages to whichever
            AI provider you have configured (OpenAI, Anthropic, Google Gemini, OpenRouter,
            or a local model via Ollama). These requests go directly from your machine to the
            provider's API — they do not pass through Crystal Lattice infrastructure.
          </p>
          <p>
            Each provider has their own privacy policy and data handling practices. If you use
            a local model via Ollama, no data leaves your machine at all.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2>The bridge service</h2>
          <p>
            Crystal Lattice includes an optional bridge service that proxies HTTP requests
            between your phone and your local server when they are on different networks.
            The bridge relays traffic in real time — it does not store your messages, sessions,
            or any conversation content. Connections are identified by a pairing code that
            you generate and your server registers. The bridge retains pairing metadata
            (a session ID and server registration) only as long as the server session is active.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2>This website</h2>
          <p>
            This website (crystallattice.dev) may collect standard web server access logs
            (IP address, browser type, pages visited, referrer) for operational purposes.
            We do not use third-party advertising trackers. If we add any analytics in the
            future, we will update this policy.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2>The mobile app</h2>
          <p>
            Crystal Lattice Control (the iOS and Android companion app) connects only to
            the server address you provide — either a local IP, an mDNS address, or the
            bridge service. The app does not transmit any data to us. It stores your
            server connection preferences locally on your device.
          </p>
          <p>
            App Store and Google Play distribution means that Apple and Google's platform
            privacy policies also apply to the download and installation of the app.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2>Open source</h2>
          <p>
            Crystal Lattice is open source under the Apache 2.0 license. You can review
            exactly what the software does by reading the source code on GitHub. There
            are no hidden network calls, no obfuscated telemetry, and no proprietary
            binary components in the core platform.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2>Changes to this policy</h2>
          <p>
            We may update this policy if the software or services change in ways that affect
            privacy. Changes will be posted to this page with an updated effective date.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2>Contact</h2>
          <p>
            Questions about this policy can be directed to the project via GitHub Issues
            or the contact information in the repository.
          </p>
        </section>
      </div>
    </div>
  </main>
  <Footer />
</Layout>

<style>
  .prose-page {
    padding: 5rem 0 6rem;
  }

  .container {
    max-width: 680px;
    margin: 0 auto;
    padding: 0 1.5rem;
  }

  .header {
    margin-bottom: 3rem;
    padding-bottom: 2rem;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border);
  }

  .label {
    font-size: 0.75rem;
    font-weight: 600;
    letter-spacing: 0.08em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--accent-soft);
    margin-bottom: 0.75rem;
  }

  h1 {
    font-size: clamp(1.75rem, 4vw, 2.5rem);
    font-weight: 700;
    letter-spacing: -0.03em;
    color: var(--text);
    margin-bottom: 0.5rem;
  }

  .meta {
    font-size: 0.875rem;
    color: var(--text-5);
  }

  .content {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 2.5rem;
  }

  section h2 {
    font-size: 1.0625rem;
    font-weight: 600;
    color: var(--text-2);
    margin-bottom: 0.75rem;
    letter-spacing: -0.01em;
  }

  section p {
    font-size: 0.9375rem;
    color: var(--text-4);
    line-height: 1.7;
    margin-bottom: 0.75rem;
  }

  section p:last-child {
    margin-bottom: 0;
  }

  section ul {
    list-style: none;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 0.5rem;
    margin-top: 0.5rem;
  }

  section ul li {
    font-size: 0.9375rem;
    color: var(--text-4);
    line-height: 1.65;
    padding-left: 1.25rem;
    position: relative;
  }

  section ul li::before {
    content: "—";
    position: absolute;
    left: 0;
    color: var(--border-strong);
  }
</style>
